WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.460
Only a handful of the world’s countries
are unscathed by the coronavirus.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.540
For the majority battling the disease
there is no single answer,

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.740
so many are testing out

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.840
different measures to fight the disease.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.130
Texas tried roadblocks to stop the spread.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.730
South Korea has aggressively 
tested for the disease.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.620
Italy has extended its emergency
anti-coronavirus

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.720
measures with a lockdown

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.460
of the entire country.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.820
Most agree keeping people at home is vital.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.140
Hong Kong has one the best records
in fighting the virus,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.060
just four deaths in a population
of seven and half million.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.580
That's not much smaller
than New York.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.840
The 2003 SARS outbreak
lives long in the memory

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.200
and the city brought in
tough early measures

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.740
to get ahead.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.440
By the end of January
Hong Kong closed schools,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.560
it sent all of its public servants home.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.320
The semiautonomous Chinese territory
is taking no chances.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.180
On March 19, the Hong Kong government began

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.160
enforcing a compulsory 14-day quarantine

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.770
for anyone arriving from overseas.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.880
Arrivals are instructed to download an app -
‘StayHomeSafe’ -

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.160
which pairs with an electronic bracelet.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.360
So far, 65,000 have been issued.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.640
While the product is new,
the technology - geofencing -

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.780
is actually pretty old.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.940
If you look at the clothes, the clothes often
has a tag on it, right?

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.660
If you leave the shop with the tag on,

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.220
the alarm will sound. 
This is geofencing.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.220
It's geofencing for the clothes.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.320
How does your application of geofencing

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.320
work in the current crisis?

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.020
Basically, in our apartment,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.900
we have different kinds
of signals beyond GPS.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.360
These signals can be wifi signals,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.120
cellular signals, 
bluetooth signals.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:54.800
So these devices offer a very rich set of
signals unique to your home.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.600
So just by learning the signature
of where you live,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.340
you know whether the person
is inside a place or not.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.040
Like a virtual boundary.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.880
Yes, it's like a virtual boundary

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.880
Some people worry about the privacy implications
of tracking people,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.920
but you said that actually

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.820
this is privacy preserving to a certain degree?

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.480
Your location is not being recorded.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.540
It's only that you are inside the home or outside.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.760
So as long as you're inside,
the government would be happy,

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.600
they're not checking where
you are exactly,

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.560
so long as you're inside the quarantine place.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.480
Once you are stepping
out, alert will be given to the government.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.800
There have been several reports of the wristbands
failing.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.700
Despite this, it’s believed many of
Hong Kong’s positive outcomes

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.980
are due to conscientious citizens
supporting tough government measures.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.090
The coronavirus has raised difficult questions

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.220
about our freedom and privacy

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.820
when the health of a population
is at severe risk.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.860
In Hong Kong, breaking your quarantine could
result in a hefty fine,

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.230
jail time or even

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.700
being shipped off to a government facility.

